00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:57,657
They're pushing each other
as hard as they can now,

248
00:14:57,740 --> 00:15:00,397
so that no matter which
one of them wins this duel,

249
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:03,009
he'll be at his best
when he faces Pegasus.

250
00:15:05,380 --> 00:15:09,117
It seems I'm the only one
who appreciates watching two

251
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:11,857
friends push each other to
the brink of their abilities.

252
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:14,820
I guess it's something
of an acquired taste.

253
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:18,957
So even though they're being
forced to fight against each other,

254
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:23,060
they've actually found a way to
help each other. It's amazing.

255
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:24,650
Whoa.

256
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,110
Okay.

257
00:15:27,193 --> 00:15:28,023
Come on, Decky.

258
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,179
Don't fail me now.

259
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:32,750
Copycat.

260
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:36,510
Ah.

261
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:38,630
All right.

262
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:40,547
I got the Grave Robber, too.

263
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:42,637
I think I could use
these two in a way that

264
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:45,197
it'd be able to take out
Yugi's Dragon Champion.

265
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:46,927
Maybe even clinch the match.

266
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:48,640
All right, Yugi.

267
00:15:48,940 --> 00:15:50,469
Ready or not, here I come.

268
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:59,520
I think this combo of
mine might actually work.

269
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:04,880
What could Joey be smiling about?

270
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:08,654
Gaia the Dragon Champion is
one of my toughest monsters.

271
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:10,450
Yu-Gi!

272
00:16:10,533 --> 00:16:12,460
Your Dragon Champ's done for.

273
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:13,980
Watch this.

274
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,300
He's done for?

275
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,676
Joey must have something big planned.

276
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:22,047
First, I'm summoning the Red-Eyes
Black Dragon in attack mode.

277
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:33,520
And I'll add Grave Robber to steal
a monster from your graveyard.

278
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:35,240
My skull?

279
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:39,449
Yeah, that's right, Yu-Gi.

280
00:16:39,700 --> 00:16:40,620
Now he's mine.

281
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:43,450
No!

282
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:47,900
And next, I think I'll throw down
this little critter right here.

283
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:51,240
Check out the copycat cards!

284
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:54,940
Now I can copy any card
you have on the field.

285
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:58,537
And I know just which one I want, too.

286
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:02,920
The powerful, mystical,
magical polymerization.

287
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,340
My fusion card. Bingo.

288
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:10,860
I may have never played it before, but
I've seen you use it plenty of times. Huh?

289
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:15,620
Red-Eyes, Black Dragon, and Summon
Skull, combine yourselves into one.

290
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:29,630
Whoa!

291
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:35,680
Check it out, the Black
Skull Dragon. Oh, no!

292
00:17:38,380 --> 00:17:42,080
Superb, two-fused duel
monsters set for battle, great.

293
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:43,720
All right, buddy.

294
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:48,293
I'm pretty sure you know what's coming
next, so you better brace yourself.

295
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:50,520
Go, Black Skull Dragon!

296
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:52,780
Attack the Dragon Champion now!

297
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:54,780
Molten Fireball!

298
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,180
I did it!

299
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:08,540
I can't believe I actually did it!

300
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:12,117
I just took down one of the most
powerful monsters in your whole deck!

301
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,141
I just beat your Dragon Champion!

302
00:18:15,780 --> 00:18:16,880
You gotta admit,

303
00:18:17,100 --> 00:18:19,517
Yook, that was a pretty
sweet move I played,

304
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:22,188
with the whole
polymerization thing and all.

305
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:28,460
I get it.

306
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:32,620
You got your game face on to try
and keep me in suspense, huh, Yugi?

307
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:34,700
No, Joey.

308
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,353
I'm just letting you enjoy your triumph.

309
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:41,040
You played a fine move, and
now allow me to play mine.

310
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:42,540
Uh-oh, guys.

311
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:45,036
I think this duel's heating up again.

312
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:47,889
Yeah, did you see that
look in Yugi's eyes?

313
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:52,460
That stare's meant doom for many
a duelist at the same time. What?

314
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:55,820
Joey seems to be almost
unstoppable right now.

315
00:18:56,080 --> 00:18:57,900
It's truly anyone's duel.

316
00:18:58,620 --> 00:19:00,420
Yu-Gi. Joey.

317
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:04,690
Bravo.

318
00:19:04,773 --> 00:19:08,240
I so look forward to seeing
how this will turn out.

319
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:10,480
Ready, pal?

320
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:13,377
Because my Black Skull Dragon's
about to end this match.

321
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:14,290
Wrong.

322
00:19:14,373 --> 00:19:16,161
This duel's just getting started.
